InfraWorldWide dataset: terms by path
=====================================

The code in this repository is MIT; see ../LICENSE. This file covers the data.
Three sets of terms apply, because the files have three different origins, and
mixing them under one licence would either give away rights that are not mine
or impose conditions on material that carries none.


1. Route geometry: Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
---------------------------------------------------

    data/geo/ro/**, data/geo/bg/**, data/geo/rs/**

and, in a build, the files those become. Named, not templated: two other
files sit in the same directory and are not OpenStreetMap data.

    public/data/geo/ro.geojson
    public/data/geo/bg.geojson
    public/data/geo/rs.geojson
    public/data/geo/cities/*.geojson
    public/data/geo/projects/*.geojson

These lines are stitched from OpenStreetMap route relations by
scripts/fetch-osm-geometry.ts. That makes them a Derivative Database of
OpenStreetMap, so OpenStreetMap's licence carries over and I cannot relax it.
Full text in LICENSE-ODbL-1.0.txt, or at
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Reusing the geometry means two things. Any work you make from it, a map image
or a page, must carry a notice that a reader can find:

    © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL

And publishing an altered version of the geometry itself means publishing it
under ODbL too, in a form somebody can take away and use.


2. Country outlines: public domain
----------------------------------

    data/geo/countries/*.geojson
    public/data/geo/countries.geojson

Natural Earth 1:50m admin-0, which is public domain. No conditions and no
attribution required, though the courtesy is welcome. These are the map's
click targets and dimming mask, and they are not OpenStreetMap data: keeping
them separate is why the ODbL obligation above stays confined to the routes.


3. Everything else: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
-------------------------------------------------------------------

    data/projects/**
    data/*.json
    and everything else the build writes under public/data/, which is the
    compiled tables, geo/cities.geojson and geo/manifest.json

Copyright (c) 2026 Simon Slănină and the InfraWorldWide contributors,
licensed CC BY 4.0. Full text in LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt, or at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Use it for anything, including commercially, as long as you credit the source
and say if you changed it. A credit that works:

    Data from InfraWorldWide (https://infraworldwide.com), CC BY 4.0

CC BY 4.0 is chosen rather than ODbL here because these records are not
derived from OpenStreetMap, so nothing forces share-alike on them, and because
it grants the two rights that actually exist over a curated collection of
facts: copyright in the descriptions and notes, and the European sui generis
database right in the compilation. Individual facts are owned by nobody. A
date, a length or a contract value can be restated by anyone without asking.


What is not mine to license
---------------------------

Figures inside these files were transcribed from public sources, and each file
names its own in a `sources` block. Those sources keep their own terms, which
are listed with the notice each one asks for in ATTRIBUTION.md. The CC BY
grant above covers my compilation and my writing, not the underlying material
of a third party.

Descriptions and notes are written from the facts a source states, not copied
from it. Wikipedia articles are CC BY-SA, which covers their wording and
structure but not the figures in them, and no sentence here is lifted or
translated from one. Contributors are held to the same rule; see
../CONTRIBUTING.md.


Scope in time
-------------

The dataset has had one author to date, so these terms apply to every
revision in the repository's history and not only to the current one. A
later contributor keeps the copyright in what they add and offers it under
the same terms; see ../CONTRIBUTING.md.
